-- db/seed-data.sql — SNAPSHOT of the processed factor set.
--
-- Generated from the live development database with:
--   docker exec calamity-db pg_dump -U calamity -d calamity --data-only --inserts \
--     --no-owner --table=public.factors --table=public.citations \
--     --table=public.factor_revisions --table=public.projections
--
-- Unlike db/seed.sql (generated from shared/seed.ts, guaranteeing parity with
-- seed mode), this is a capture of the INGESTED and PROCESSED set: everything
-- the pipeline found, the reputability gate admitted, and the backfills scored —
-- significance bands, closesWindow judgements, quantity thresholds, and the
-- projections that date them.
--
-- APPLYING THIS REPLACES, IT DOES NOT MERGE. An earlier revision used
-- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, which is right for a fresh database and useless for
-- an existing one: every row already present kept its old values, so a target
-- that already had the factors gained none of the re-scoring. Load it via
-- db/apply-seed-data.sql, which truncates the four tables inside one
-- transaction first.
--
-- Embeddings ARE included. They are most of the file's size, but restoring
-- without them leaves dedupe silently degraded until a full re-embed, which
-- costs real money — a bigger file is the cheaper failure.
--
-- PostgreSQL database dump
--

